Usage: cli check-pick-entered [OPTIONS]

  DM if today's delivered pick was never entered in the MLB app.

  Each watchdog CLI invocation attempts to publish one entry receipt and its seal.

  v2 (2026-07-03, RE-ENABLED in cron): entry is now detected from the UNION of two sources — the profile
  endpoint (settled rows only; v1's sole source and why v1 false-alarmed every pre-pitch day and was
  disabled 2026-06-12) and GET api/predictions (discovered via the app JS bundle), which exposes the
  pending same-day row before settlement. Any fetch failure skips quietly WITHOUT consuming the once-per-
  day marker, so a transient error can never produce the v1 false-alarm class — the next cron run
  retries.

  The installed watchdog launches every 15 minutes ET. It prints the outcome when it skips a check. An
  eligible early check uses the dated early ledger. Manual and original-hours checks use the live ledger.
  While eligible, an unresolved entry is checked again, with throttled reminders at 30 and 15 minutes to
  cutoff and an all-clear when a warned entry is confirmed.

Options:
  --picks-dir TEXT          Picks directory
  --expected-username TEXT  Refuse if session identity differs
  --dm-recipient TEXT       Bluesky handle for the not-entered DM
  --window-min INTEGER      Check only within this many minutes before first pitch
  --now-et TEXT             Test override: naive ET datetime ISO
  --cron                    Before 10:00 ET, defer an in-window check of a committed pick if a nominal
                            10:00–23:45 ET quarter-hour is also inside that window.
  --help                    Show this message and exit.

check-pick-entered: early check deferred because a nominal 10:00–23:45 ET quarter-hour is inside this pick's entry window
